{
  "summary": "This experiment tested the first multimodal configuration by adding ResNet50 image features with simple concat fusion to the proven best RNA pipeline (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool), achieving a validation accuracy of 0.632 and F1 of 0.607. This is slightly below the RNA-only best (0.650 acc / 0.628 F1), indicating that the addition of ResNet50 image features via concat fusion does not provide incremental predictive value over the strong RNA representation and may introduce a small amount of noise. It remains uncertain whether alternative fusion strategies (e.g., weighted or attention-based) or different image encoders (e.g., ViT) could extract complementary signal from the image modality, or whether the image features are fundamentally uninformative for this classification task."
}

